    "innovation": "This paper provides a comprehensive synthesis of knowledge on carbon dioxide emissions from fossil-fuel combustion, covering calculation methods, global inventories, spatiotemporal distribution, atmospheric transport, and associated uncertainties to summarize the state of understanding on the topic.",
    "kg_extraction_triplets": [
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "CT2007",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_SUBSEQUENT_VERSION",
            "target_entity_instance": "CT2007B",
            "target_entity_type": "Source",
            "paragraph": "Between the original CT2007 and subsequent CT2007B release, new CDIAC FFCO2 emissions inventory data became available (including not only the addition of another year of data but also revisions of data from previous years). For the entire period 2000\u20132005, the global FFCO2 emissions used in CT2007B were higher than those from CT2007. One prominent difference in CT2007B compared to CT2007 was an increase in the estimate of the FFCO2 emissions in Asia (primarily China, Fig. 6a).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "CT2007B",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_SUBSEQUENT_VERSION",
            "target_entity_instance": "CT2008",
            "target_entity_type": "Source",
            "paragraph": "The second significant revision in CT FFCO2 emissions has to do with a change applied between the CT2007B and CT2008 releases. Since the CT2007B release, CT monthly FFCO2 emissions for each pixel have been set to evolve smoothly in time, using a flux-conserving spline interpolation scheme that yields minimal temporal discontinuities while exactly preserving annual total emissions (Fig. 6b).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
